-- the general form, because two regimes rest on it in opposite directions: a relation on anything at
-- all, with an instance of its failure to compose. For biosimilars the relation under-licenses — each
-- pairwise comparison to the reference holds and no chain of substitutions is covered. For the
-- Federal Analogue Act it over-licenses: 21 U.S.C. 802(32) makes a substance criminal when its
-- "chemical structure is substantially similar to" a scheduled one, with no criterion given, and the
-- consequence is transported along that relation as though it were identity.
NonTransitiveAt : (A : Type 1) → (A → A → Type 0) → Type 1
NonTransitiveAt A R = (x : A) × (y : A) × (z : A) × R x y × R y z × (R x z → Empty)
